1
00:00:00,167 --> 00:00:02,700
Life doesn't always go according to plan.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,267
An unexpected expense, an uncertain market,

3
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:08,367
or simply a change in priorities can make you rethink your SIP.

4
00:00:08,367 --> 00:00:10,100
But before you make that change,

5
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:13,767
wouldn't it help to understand what it means for your planned contributions?

6
00:00:16,167 --> 00:00:18,533
Meet Skip Check by FinLit Ventures.

7
00:00:18,533 --> 00:00:22,667
A simple way to compare your options before deciding what works for you.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,800
Say your monthly SIP is twelve thousand rupees,

9
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:31,433
and you're considering reducing it to six thousand for six months.

10
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:35,900
That's thirty-six thousand rupees less in planned contributions over that period.

11
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:41,867
That's a contribution difference,

12
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:45,200
not an investment loss or a prediction of future returns.

13
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:49,167
Your existing units remain invested unless you separately redeem them.

14
00:00:49,167 --> 00:00:51,300
Keep, reduce, or pause.

15
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,900
Review the difference, understand the trade-off,

16
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:56,000
and choose what fits your situation.

17
00:01:00,833 --> 00:01:01,900
Skip Check.

18
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,133
See the difference.

19
00:01:03,133 --> 00:01:04,433
Make your decision.
